abstract: >-
  Pre-registered study of how residual-stream updates travel through depth in
  transformer factual recall. Cross-layer updates are predictable (largely an
  architectural property) but not depth-stationary, which points to a
  first-order, depth-indexed state-space model; the causal test returns a clean
  null. Code is MIT-licensed; the paper, protocol, figures and run records are
  CC BY 4.0.
